      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Faced same issue after upgrading to Windows 11. Clicking anywhere on VRChat window with Touch controller laser using Oculus Dash crashing Dash and controller buttons/thumbsticks stopping working in VRChat. Clicking on VRChat window with hardware mouse cursor with Dash open does not crash it.\n\nBoth SteamVR and Oculus store VRChat versions are affected by this issue.\n\nAlso both Oculus Rift CV1 and Oculus Quest 1 are affected (tested Quest 1 with Quest Link cable and Oculus Store VRChat version)\n\nCrash does not happen when loading VRChat in local test mode without EAC OR if I run VRChat as administrator.\n\nTried reinstalling/repairing VRChat, EAC, Nvidia drivers, Oculus software, also tried v63 beta of Oculus software.\n\nWhen crash happening these lines appear in oculus Service log file:\n\n02/03 18:17:05.938 {!ERROR!} [Dash] [dash_error] { message: \"[S]: Hang detected on Main Thread (2 seconds)\\r\\n\",  }\n\n02/03 18:17:05.938 {INFO}    [LifeCycle] set_dash_rendering_blocked() Start\n\n02/03 18:17:05.938 {WARNING} [LifeCycle] Dash rendering is blocked. Deadlocked: true, Tracking Failure: false\n\n02/03 18:17:05.938 {INFO}    [LifeCycle] updateSDKFocus focusedTrackerPid: 26448 (C_Steam_steamapps_common_SteamVR_bin_win32_vrstartup)\n\n02/03 18:17:05.938 {INFO}    [LifeCycle] Already Focused: 26448 (C_Steam_steamapps_common_SteamVR_bin_win32_vrstartup)\n\n02/03 18:17:05.938 {INFO}    [LifeCycle] set_dash_rendering_blocked() End\n\nSystem specs:\n\nIntel i7-12700K\n\nNvidia RTX 2080\n\nOculus Rift CV1 and Oculus Quest 1\n\nRunning VRChat through SteamVR\n\nVRChat version 2024.1.1p1, build 1405\n\nWindows 11 23H2\n\nGPU Driver version 551.61",
